      "writtenOn": "2026-10-14T01:37:07Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Taking a closer look, I think I was wrong. I now believe the libvpx encoder supports a flipped input image, even though those two lines in `image2yuvconfig()` do not.\n\nThe input image to the libvpx encoder is converted twice.\n\nThe first conversion is done by the `image2yuvconfig()` function.\n\nThe second conversion is done by the `vp9_copy_and_extend_frame()` function.\n\nAfter the second conversion, the input image, if originally flipped, is flipped back. So subsequently the libvpx encoder always deals with a non-flipped input image.",
      "parentUuid": "fabb0e1a_b5f769fb",
      "revId": "79fdc54cad07b7aaf241c559be59493746e43c72",
      "serverId": "3ce6091f-6c88-37e8-8c75-72f92ae8dfba"
